{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHeckeMTC","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneHeckeMTC","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.BWVacuumRowIsHecke","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneModularTwist","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge"],"declarations":28,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.conjugate_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.conjugate_nil","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeMTC.lean#L212-L213","doc":"`Partition.conjugate [] = []` — the empty diagram is self-conjugate (no columns). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.heckeMTC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.heckeMTC","kind":"def","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeMTC.lean#L176-L210","doc":"**The Hecke q-dimensions + ribbon twist realize `HeckeMTC`** for `q > 1` on any conjugate-closed\nset `P` of weakly-decreasing blocks containing the empty (vacuum) partition. `qDim := d_q`,\n`theta := θ_λ = q^{c(λ)}`, `D := √(Σ d_q²)`, `S0 := d_q/D`, `vac := []`.\n\nThe two modular-data inputs are discharged from the **corpus proofs**, not carried abstractly:\n`qDim_conj` from `QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.qDim_conj` and `theta_conj` from\n`QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.theta_conjugate`. `D ≠ 0` reuses `KeystoneVerlindeSMatrixBridge.sum_qDimSq_pos`\n(positivity, `q > 1`). `S0_eq` is `rfl`.\n\nThe **only** thing this does *not* establish is the physics — that the BW localization of `S³/2I`\nactually *is* this category (`bwse` / bean `bwhk`); that owner-gated identification is the open\nresidual. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.verlindeMeasure_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.verlindeMeasure_conj","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeMTC.lean#L165-L170","doc":"**The Verlinde measure is transpose-invariant: `μ(λ′) = μ(λ)`.** Immediate from `S0_conj` — the\nPlancherel weight is chirality-blind. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.verlindeMeasure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.verlindeMeasure","kind":"def","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeMTC.lean#L162-L163","doc":"**The Verlinde measure** `μ(λ) = S₀(λ)²` of the target MTC. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.theta_conj_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.theta_conj_mul","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeMTC.lean#L154-L160","doc":"**The twist's chirality law in product form: `θ(λ′)·θ(λ) = 1`.** Derived from the `theta_conj`\nfield (`θ_{λ′} = θ_λ⁻¹`) and `θ(λ) ≠ 0`. The bar-involution pairs `V_λ` with its dual `V_{λ′}` so their\nframing anomalies cancel — the modular `T`-matrix's charge-conjugation compatibility. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.S0_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.S0_conj","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeMTC.lean#L147-L152","doc":"**The vacuum row is chirality-blind (transpose-invariant): `S₀(λ′) = S₀(λ)`.** Derived from the\n`qDim_conj` field (the corpus-proved `d_q(λ′) = d_q(λ)`) via `S₀ = d_q/D` — the `S`-matrix's\n`C₂`-analogue (invariant, complementing the twist's inverting `θ_{λ′} = θ_λ⁻¹`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.S0_eq_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.S0_eq_smul","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeMTC.lean#L139-L145","doc":"**The vacuum row as a `1/D`-rescaling of the quantum dimension**, `S₀(λ) = (1/D)·d_q(λ)`, via the\ncorpus-proved `VerlindeVacuumRow.S0_eq_smul` (no per-block freedom — the single normalisation `1/D`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.S0_ratio_eq_qDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.S0_ratio_eq_qDim","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeMTC.lean#L129-L137","doc":"**The `S`-matrix vacuum-row modular datum (`S₀ = d_q/D`), via `VerlindeVacuumRow`.** The\nvacuum-row ratio to the vacuum entry recovers the quantum dimension:\n`S₀(λ) / S₀(vac) = d_q(λ)`. Proved by transporting the corpus-proved\n`QOU.BraidKnot.VerlindeVacuumRow.S0_ratio` through the `S0_eq` identity `S₀ = d_q/D`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.toVerlindeVacuumRow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.toVerlindeVacuumRow","kind":"def","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeMTC.lean#L118-L127","doc":"**Reuse bridge** — the `HeckeMTC`'s vacuum-`S`-row data as a `VerlindeVacuumRow`\n([`BWVacuumRowIsHecke.lean`](BWVacuumRowIsHecke.lean)): `d := qDim`, `D := D`, `vac := vac`. Lets the\ncorpus-proved `VerlindeVacuumRow.S0_ratio` / `S0_eq_smul` discharge the `S`-matrix relations without\nre-deriving `S₀ = d_q/D`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.S0_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.S0_eq","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeMTC.lean#L112-L112","doc":"**Published modular-data identity** `S₀(λ) = d_q(λ)/D` (vacuum row of the `S`-matrix in any MTC). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.S0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.S0","kind":"def","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeMTC.lean#L110-L110","doc":"The **vacuum `S`-matrix row** `S₀(λ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.D_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.D_sq","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeMTC.lean#L108-L108","doc":"`D² = Σ_λ d_q(λ)²` — the defining global-dimension relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.D_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.D_ne","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeMTC.lean#L106-L106","doc":"`D ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.D","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.D","kind":"def","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeMTC.lean#L104-L104","doc":"The global quantum dimension `D` (total dimension of the modular category). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.theta_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.theta_conj","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeMTC.lean#L102-L102","doc":"**Corpus-proved input** — the twist's chirality law `θ_{λ′} = θ_λ⁻¹`\n(`QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.theta_conjugate`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.theta_vac","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.theta_vac","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeMTC.lean#L99-L99","doc":"The twist is trivial on the vacuum: `θ_vac = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.theta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.theta","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeMTC.lean#L97-L97","doc":"The ribbon twist / modular `T`-matrix eigenvalue `θ_λ` (diagonal modular datum). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.qDim_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.qDim_conj","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeMTC.lean#L95-L95","doc":"**Corpus-proved input** `d_q(λ′) = d_q(λ)` (`QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityI.qDim_conj`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.qDim_vac","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.qDim_vac","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeMTC.lean#L93-L93","doc":"The vacuum object has quantum dimension `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.qDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.qDim","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeMTC.lean#L91-L91","doc":"The categorical quantum dimension `d_q(λ)` of the Hecke block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.vac_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.vac_mem","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeMTC.lean#L89-L89","doc":"The vacuum is one of the blocks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.vac","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.vac","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeMTC.lean#L87-L87","doc":"The monoidal unit / vacuum object. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.conj_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.conj_mem","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeMTC.lean#L85-L85","doc":"The blocks are closed under transpose. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.conj","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeMTC.lean#L83-L83","doc":"The transpose (bar / charge-conjugation) involution `λ ↦ λ′`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.parts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.parts","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeMTC.lean#L81-L81","doc":"The finite set of Hecke partition blocks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.Part","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.Part","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeMTC.lean#L79-L79","doc":"Partition index for the Hecke block `λ ⊢ n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC.mk","kind":"ctor","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeMTC.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.HeckeMTC","kind":"structure","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneHeckeMTC.lean#L60-L112","doc":"**The Hecke/Temperley–Lieb side as a concrete modular tensor category (the target of \"BW = Hecke\").**\n\nBundles both pieces of modular data on the Hecke partition blocks:\n\n* the **vacuum `S`-matrix row** `S0 : Part → R` with the published modular-data identity\n  `S₀(λ) = d_q(λ)/D` (`S0_eq`), and a distinguished vacuum object `vac` of quantum dimension `1`;\n* the **ribbon twist / modular `T`-matrix** `theta : Part → R`, diagonal, with the chirality law\n  `θ_{λ′} = θ_λ⁻¹` (`theta_conj`) and `θ_vac = 1`;\n\ntogether with the quantum dimension `qDim = d_q` (transpose-invariant, `qDim_conj`), the global\ndimension `D` (`D² = Σ d_q²`, `D_sq`; `D ≠ 0`, `D_ne`), and the transpose (bar) involution `conj`\nclosing the block set (`conj_mem`).\n\nThe fields `qDim_conj`, `theta_conj`, `S0_eq`, `D_sq` are the modular-data *inputs*; the file's theorems\n*derive* the modular-data consequences from them. Constructing an instance whose `qDim` is the *Hecke*\n`d_q` and whose `S0` is the *BW gauge datum* is the open physics content (`bwse` / bean `bwhk`), NOT\nsupplied by this class. ","signatureChunk":0}]}